# Source coverage and implementation status

Use this page to check what "covered" means before you claim that Civica supports a pattern. Coverage means there is local guidance and either an example or an explicit replacement. It does not mean the pattern is installed in native Home Assistant.

The page is for maintainers and reviewers. It maps every entry in the reviewed GOV.UK component index, the NHS component and pattern indexes and the Publishing Design Guide. That includes nested publishing-template variants and the NHS review-date entry, which is now withdrawn.

## Read the status correctly

State which status you mean. Otherwise a reader may take a design reference for a working feature.

| Status | What it establishes | What it does not establish |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Maintained theme or companion | Named implementation in this repository, with stated compatibility and checks | Universal support for every Home Assistant card |
| Reference component or pattern | An authored, inspectable design with usage and testing guidance | A connected backend, device action or native HA replacement |
| Withdrawn source | A recorded source decision and a recommended replacement | A recommendation to build the obsolete component |

A documentation control proves only the behaviour of its local example. A claim about live Home Assistant needs separate installation and route checks. The examples use invented data and local actions.

## Source inventories

These counts are evidence: each row is the number of entries in the index reviewed on the dates recorded in the coverage record.

| Source | Reviewed entries | Local organisation |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| [GOV.UK components](https://design-system.service.gov.uk/components/) | 37 | Shared atomic components, with Civica header and footer replacements |
| [NHS components](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/components) | 38 | Forms, content presentation and navigation; cards and action links share existing guidance |
| [NHS patterns](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns) | 13 | Inclusive content, household tasks and page patterns |
| [Publishing Design Guide](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/) | 42 | 11 components, 1 search-filter pattern and 30 page-template entries, including nested variants |

Overlapping source entries share one canonical local page, so the source counts do not add up to a count of unique pages. The [dated UK systems review](uk-design-system-review.html) adds the MoJ, DWP, Home Office, ONS and Scottish Government catalogue decisions. It records detail-page review separately.

The machine-readable [coverage record](../reference/coverage.json) lists every source URL, local route and example ID. The [complete sitemap](../sitemap.html) and [search](../search.html) use the same Middleman page catalogue as section navigation.

