The [A to Z Technical lexicon](../content/style-guides/technical-a-to-z.html) records the official glossary, entity domains and selected native vocabulary. Use its stated source denominators and version boundaries. It does not claim to cover every vendor-defined integration label or future custom card.

## Adaptation decisions

These are design decisions, not source findings.

Civica does not copy NHS identity rules, clinical urgency or NHS-number collection into a household application. It uses Civica artwork, describes household consequences directly and adapts the identifier pattern to useful device and configuration identifiers. The [BSL pattern](../patterns/british-sign-language.html) sets out what signed-content availability, production and review need. It does not invent a verified household video.

Publishing ministerial, organisation, statistical and policy templates become household owners, guides, reports and collections. They keep the useful editorial structure and leave out government authority claims. Some patterns describe a future authored application. Do not infer that a native dashboard now includes a publishing backend.

